    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Manage declarative draft blueprints.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  init                        Create an empty blueprint workspace skeleton.\r\n  plan                        Show the cmd_list a future apply would execute (dry-run).\r\n  apply                       Apply the blueprint workspace onto a real draft.\r\n                              If --ref does not exist a blank draft is created;\r\n                              if it exists the workspace is treated as a diff edit.\r\n  cancel                      Request cancellation of the active blueprint apply for this\r\n                              client session.\r\n  commerce                    Extract XML-only atomic capability keys for commerce precheck.\r\n                              This command plans only; it does not execute draft edits or\r\n                              charge.\r\n  patch                       Apply a Node Patch to the latest synchronized Draft XML and write\r\n                              the result to target_draft.xml. Use --dry-run to validate without\r\n                              writing.\r\n  sync                        Reverse-sync a real draft back into blueprint XML.\r\n                              When --workspace is provided, target_draft.xml,\r\n                              current_draft.xml, and id_map.json are updated.\r\n                              Without --workspace, XML is returned in the output envelope\r\n                              and no files are written.\r\n  resource                    Process declarative material operations (--search), including\r\n                              resource search, video-frame derivation, music-beat analysis,\r\n                              standalone ASR, TTS generation, then import\r\n                              a local media file (--import). Search-only processing can also\r\n                              return JSON without a workspace.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint init  --workspace ./bp_ws --protocol xmldraft\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint plan  --workspace ./bp_ws\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint apply --workspace ./bp_ws --ref local://example --selection-file ./edit.selection\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint cancel\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint commerce --workspace ./bp_ws --selection-file ./edit.selection\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint patch --workspace ./bp_ws --patch-file ./patch.xml\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint sync  --workspace ./bp_ws --ref local://example\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint sync  --ref local://example\r\n\r\nXML TIME LITERALS\r\n  XMLDraft time values are unitless milliseconds.\r\n  Unit suffixes such as us, ms, s, min, or m are rejected.\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Use `lyra-cli draft blueprint <subcommand> --help` for more information.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Manage declarative draft blueprints.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  init                        Create an empty blueprint workspace skeleton.\r\n  plan                        Show the cmd_list a future apply would execute (dry-run).\r\n  apply                       Apply the blueprint workspace onto a real draft.\r\n                              If --ref does not exist a blank draft is created;\r\n                              if it exists the workspace is treated as a diff edit.\r\n  cancel                      Request cancellation of the active blueprint apply for this\r\n                              client session.\r\n  commerce                    Extract XML-only atomic capability keys for commerce precheck.\r\n                              This command plans only; it does not execute draft edits or\r\n                              charge.\r\n  patch                       Apply a Node Patch to the latest synchronized Draft XML and write\r\n                              the result to target_draft.xml. Use --dry-run to validate without\r\n                              writing.\r\n  sync                        Reverse-sync a real draft back into blueprint XML.\r\n                              When --workspace is provided, target_draft.xml,\r\n                              current_draft.xml, and id_map.json are updated.\r\n                              Without --workspace, XML is returned in the output envelope\r\n                              and no files are written.\r\n  resource                    Process declarative material operations (--search), including\r\n                              resource search, video-frame derivation, music-beat analysis,\r\n                              standalone ASR, TTS generation, then import\r\n                              a local media file (--import). Search-only processing can also\r\n                              return JSON without a workspace.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint init  --workspace ./bp_ws --protocol xmldraft\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint plan  --workspace ./bp_ws\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint apply --workspace ./bp_ws --ref local://example --selection-file ./edit.selection\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint cancel\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint commerce --workspace ./bp_ws --selection-file ./edit.selection\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint patch --workspace ./bp_ws --patch-file ./patch.xml\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint sync  --workspace ./bp_ws --ref local://example\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft blueprint sync  --ref local://example\r\n\r\nXML TIME LITERALS\r\n  XMLDraft time values are unitless milliseconds.\r\n  Unit suffixes such as us, ms, s, min, or m are rejected.\r\n\r\nLEARN MORE\r\n  Use `lyra-cli draft blueprint <subcommand> --help` for more information.\r\n",
